    "body": "<!-- linear-linkback -->\n<details>\n<summary><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4684/cc3-s8ddfb1-okr-desktop-macos-a-flow-alert-clicked-from-notification\">TXE-4684 [CC3-s8ddfb1] OKR desktop (macOS): a Flow alert clicked from Notification Center after its banner has hidden never reaches the app, so the click opens nothing</a></summary>\n<p>\n\nDeliverable consumer: OKR desktop users on macOS who click a Flow or mention alert after its banner has left the screen.\n\n## What happens\n\nFound in the [TXE-4409](https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4409/cc-codex-abd3592cbfc8-flow-feature-complete-composed-acceptance) installed acceptance on 2026-10-20 (test package `dev.txe.okr.desktop.e2e-txe4402`, built from eb6e77d663586cf1307b7c820a735b7c4359a580, ad hoc, the only LaunchServices registration of that bundle id).\n\nAttempt 4 (`~/.cache/okr-flow-cc3/txe-4409/installed-20261020T125942Z/`, macOS unified log in `macos-log/`):\n\n* 13:00:40.160Z: the running app (pid 16309) adds notification request ident 73EA-0461 for alert 8679de69-a046-470c-ac72-1d87caa0c134. usernoted logs \"Presenting … as banner\" at 13:00:40.163Z. The app logs alert-received, alert-shown and alert-acked.\n* 13:03:35.002Z: usernoted logs \"Received response\" for that same request, then \"Bringing app dev.txe.okr.desktop.e2e-txe4402 front for response\" with the correct package URL. WindowServer makes pid 16309 frontmost at 13:03:39.520Z. No second instance is launched.\n* The app never logs `alert-clicked`, so it opens no route. The person clicked and nothing opened.\n\nAttempt 3, with the same package and the same alert path, shows the contrast. There the click came 67 s after display: `alert-clicked` (sameSession true) at 12:57:54.795Z, and T1 opened. In attempt 4 the click came 175 s after display, when the banner had already gone to Notification Center.\n\n## Hypothesis (not yet proved)\n\n`okr/desktop/src/shell/alerts.cjs` `nativeNotifier` keeps each Notification in the `live` set so it is not garbage-collected. It deletes the object on a `close` event whose reason is not `timedOut`. If Electron on macOS emits `close` when the banner leaves the screen, the object can be collected. A later click from Notification Center then has no JS listener: macOS activates the app, but `click` never fires.\n\n## Done when\n\n* A test reproduces the loss through the real `nativeNotifier` path: a click delivered after a `close` that is not a dismissal. The test fails on main.\n* The minimal fix keeps every shown notification clickable until it is clicked, explicitly dismissed by the person, or replaced. Any other lifetime limit must be bounded and stated.\n* The test runs in a CI suite.\n* A clicked-late alert opens its route in an installed-package check, with evidence.\n* The \"macOS took it\" (`alert-shown`) semantics stay unchanged.\n\nSource ownership: `alerts.cjs` may be under a Notification Center lease. The FL-15 coordinator coordinates that before any product edit.\n</p>\n</details>\n<!-- linear-review-link -->\n<p><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/review/cc3-s8ddfb1-fixokr-txe-4684-a-notification-center-click-routed-to-a-5aee04969f4f\">Review in Linear</a></p>\n",
